Third-party components
================================================================================

Ren'Py
------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Role:     Target engine. renmori protects games built with Ren'Py and
            repacks the engine runtime. renmori is not affiliated with or
            endorsed by the Ren'Py project.
  License:  Ren'Py is distributed under a liberal (MIT-like) license, with
            some bundled components under their own terms (LGPL, etc.).
  Action:   Preserve Ren'Py's own license and notices when repacking the
            engine into a protected distribution.
  URL:      https://www.renpy.org/

FFmpeg                                                              [LANDMINE]
------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Role:     Video/audio decoding, as bundled by Ren'Py. renmori feeds it
            decrypted streams through the loader; it does not modify FFmpeg.
  License:  LGPL-2.1+ (some builds/configurations are GPL).
  Action:   COMPLIANCE-CRITICAL. LGPL requires that the end user be able to
            replace the FFmpeg library. Our protection must not break that
            relinking ability for FFmpeg specifically, and we must not
            statically bind FFmpeg into a form that defeats LGPL relinking.
            Verify the license of the exact FFmpeg build shipped. Carry
            FFmpeg's license text and source-offer as required.
  URL:      https://ffmpeg.org/legal.html

